# Stage 1 — twenty-eight provisional directions from the catalogue

**Historical stage-1 record: superseded by the completed full-available-abstract analysis in `MINING-FINDINGS.md`.**

**This first pass was not abstract mining.** I independently read all 1,114 dated title/topic rows in the collected catalogue. All abstract fields are null; no episode audio or full discussion was reviewed. These are original design questions suggested by topics, not summaries of broadcasts. The requested complete abstract collection is still unresolved.

Catalogue: Wikipedia contributors, [revision 1382152739](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_In_Our_Time_programmes?oldid=1382152739), CC BY-SA 4.0. Snapshot includes 1,109 aired substantive entries, three presenter specials and two future listings. The 28 selected leads below are aired Bragg-era discussions. No episode maps automatically to a chapter.

## What the full scan changed

- **Materials are intellectual history.** Glass, print, clocks and instruments provide understandable combinations that generate new evidence rather than more arithmetic.
- **Classification is a long argument.** Aristotle’s animals, Linnaeus, environmental relationships, anthropology and Borges can revisit what a category does—and what it leaves out.
- **Time is several problems.** Calendars, navigation, relativity, lived duration and branching fiction connect without being collapsed into one theory.
- **Order is not always designed.** Mandeville and complexity suggest consequences, feedback and competing public goods, useful for speculative futures.
- **A universal history needs resistance.** The Needham Question, Jaipur and translation routes can prevent the Greek tradition from being portrayed as a self-sufficient inevitable ladder.
- **Wonder does not have to lose.** Renaissance magic, dream and Surrealism can remain serious parts of the inquiry, with distinct standards for historical belief, scientific evidence and artistic invention.

## Selected leads — inspiration, not chapter slots

### 1. [The Library at Nineveh](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b00b7r71) · 2008-05-15
**The archive has a politics.** What makes scattered observations a body of knowledge? Put sky records, omen interpretation, scribal selection and royal power on the same desk.
Connection direction: Archive -> comparison -> an argument about what survives.
[Topic research](https://www.britishmuseum.org/collection/object/W_1883-0118-243). A physical royal astronomical/astrological report is documented; no claim that the whole collection was a modern public library.

### 2. [Cynicism](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p003k9js) · 2005-10-20
**A philosophy can be a way of living.** Diogenes suggests an action rather than another summary: remove a social dependency and discover the freedom—and cost—of needing less.
Connection direction: Socratic examination -> Cynic practice -> Stoic self-command; later luxury critique is a comparison unless sourced.
[Topic research](https://iep.utm.edu/cynics/). Anecdotes are transmitted literary evidence, not eyewitness transcripts.

### 3. [Aristotle's biology](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/m0002cfd) · 2019-02-07
**Classification starts with living things.** Aristotle need not be only syllogisms. Compare animal structures and ask what a part does; later classification and evolution can change that explanation.
Connection direction: Observed likeness -> kinds -> function -> adaptation.
[Topic research](https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/aristotle-biology/). Do not turn Aristotle into a modern evolutionary biologist or the first observer anywhere.

### 4. [The Music of the Spheres](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b00c1fct) · 2008-06-19
**Beauty can guide an explanation without proving it.** The attraction of a harmonious cosmos is a way to connect music, proportion and astronomy while keeping observations able to resist the beautiful model.
Connection direction: Musical order -> celestial order -> Kepler’s revision rather than arithmetic drills.
[Topic research](https://galileo.ou.edu/exhibits/music-of-the-spheres.html). Historical harmonic inquiry is not evidence that planets audibly sing.

### 5. [The Translation Movement](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b00dp4d8) · 2008-10-02
**Translation changes the questions.** A manuscript crossing languages can acquire new problems and arguments rather than simply being carried like a sealed package.
Connection direction: Greek texts + Syriac/Arabic scholarship -> original work -> Latin reception.
[Topic research](https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/arabic-islamic-influence/). Separate Greek-to-Arabic and Arabic-to-Latin routes; do not credit a single building with every translation.

### 6. [The Needham Question](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p0038x9m) · 2006-10-19
**Question the shape of the history itself.** This is a design safeguard: ask what is hidden by a story that measures every tradition against a supposedly inevitable European endpoint.
Connection direction: Paper, printing and other technical routes should disrupt a one-way ladder.
[Topic research](https://www.nri.cam.ac.uk/about/). The institute documents a research tradition; competing answers to the Needham Question remain questions, not a solved recipe.

### 7. [Optics](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b00774t5) · 2007-03-01
**Seeing is an argument.** Light entering the eye, the dark room and a checkable image can connect vision to perspective, telescopes and photography.
Connection direction: Optical account -> reproducible effect -> instrument -> new evidence.
[Topic research](https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/arabic-islamic-influence/). Specific optical transmission needs its own text-level evidence; this entry is a research lead, not proof of every link.

### 8. [The Science of Glass](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b05w456c) · 2015-05-28
**Materials can reorganize knowledge.** Glass is unusually fertile: transparent vessel, curved lens, telescope, microscope, photographic image. One material opens unrelated-looking sciences.
Connection direction: Craft -> lens -> distant/near worlds; many returns rather than a glass chapter quota.
[Topic research](https://catalogue.museogalileo.it/multimedia/LensmakingBis.html). Do not compress distinct lens and instrument inventions into one heroic event.

### 9. [The Encyclopédie](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p0038x93) · 2006-10-26
**Knowledge can be rearranged for readers.** The encyclopedic project offers a desk full of crafts and arguments with cross-references, and a live question about who gets to name the branches of knowledge.
Connection direction: Workshop knowledge + print -> public reference work -> contested classifications.
[Topic research](https://encyclopedie.uchicago.edu/). The complete historical source is available through an academic edition; game text will be authored, not bulk copied.

### 10. [Baconian Science](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b00jdb6c) · 2009-04-02
**What did Francis Bacon actually change?.** Make the player notice a negative instance, isolate a variable, and organize collaborative inquiry. This is a substantive answer to the user’s question.
Connection direction: Natural histories -> eliminative comparisons -> experiments -> cooperative research.
[Topic research](https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/francis-bacon/). Bacon neither invented all experiment nor supplied the unique modern scientific method.

### 11. [Renaissance Magic](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p004y28n) · 2004-06-17
**Magic and experiment need not be opposites.** Natural magic can keep wonder, hidden causes, optical effects and practical making together. It prevents a false superstition-to-reason march.
Connection direction: Della Porta’s optical effects can connect old cosmologies and new instruments without erasing either.
[Topic research](https://galileo.ou.edu/exhibits/natural-magick-1658.html). Natural magic is historically situated inquiry, not endorsement of supernatural mechanisms.

### 12. [The Invention of Photography](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b07j699g) · 2016-07-07
**An image can become a trace.** A projected image plus a light-sensitive surface is an immediately intelligible synthesis. Its later effect on art and evidence need not be another measuring exercise.
Connection direction: Camera obscura -> fixed photograph -> questions of framing, realism and art.
[Topic research](https://www.hrc.utexas.edu/niepce-heliograph/). Photography has multiple inventors and processes; a fixed image is not automatically an objective interpretation.

### 13. [The Observatory at Jaipur](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b00hmpdd) · 2009-02-19
**The sky is not a single European workshop.** Jaipur offers an active meeting of astronomical traditions and instruments, not an exotic interruption. Architecture itself can become an observing instrument.
Connection direction: Translated tables + local observations + monumental instruments -> correction.
[Topic research](https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1338). Verify the particular texts and people before asserting a direct transmission route.

### 14. [Longitude](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/m000vyn6) · 2021-05-13
**A clock becomes a position.** Reference time and local noon make longitude conceptually graspable. Mechanical timekeepers and lunar observations remain alternative systems with different requirements.
Connection direction: Astronomy + clocks + sea trials -> navigation; trade and coercion are not erased.
[Topic research](https://www.rmg.co.uk/stories/time/harrisons-clocks-longitude-problem). No numerical longitude problem; no simple lone-genius versus foolish-establishment myth.

### 15. [Humboldt](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p003c1c2) · 2006-09-28
**A collection becomes a connected landscape.** Humboldt makes a different synthesis from taxonomy: altitude, climate and plant distribution can become a patterned whole.
Connection direction: Specimen labels -> environmental relations -> ecology.
[Topic research](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41559-019-0980-5). Recognize collaborators and local knowledge; do not present one European as discovering that nature is connected.

### 16. [Linnaeus](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/m001l291) · 2023-04-20
**Names help—and can carry prejudice.** Classification creates a powerful shared tool but invites questions about which distinctions are useful and which rankings are imposed.
Connection direction: Aristotelian kinds -> Linnaean naming -> evolutionary trees; human hierarchy remains criticizable.
[Topic research](https://www.linnean.org/learning/who-was-linnaeus/linnaeus-and-race). Do not repeat historical racial classifications as biological truths.

### 17. [The Origins of Infectious Disease](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b011pldm) · 2011-06-09
**World history needs multiple causes.** Disease connects organisms, settlements, animals and routes of contact. It can complicate macrohistory without turning geography or germs into destiny.
Connection direction: Microscopy + public records + contact networks -> mechanisms and unequal exposure.
[Topic research](https://www.cdc.gov/museum/history/). This is a research direction, not verified coverage of the broadcast; colonial epidemic claims need separate historical sources.

### 18. [The Anatomy of Melancholy](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b010y30m) · 2011-05-12
**The crowded desk can be the subject.** Burton is an antidote to sterile research summaries: inherited medicine, philosophy, literary examples and first-person experience gather in a deliberately sprawling book.
Connection direction: Ancient temperaments -> Renaissance reading -> later questions about mind and interpretation.
[Topic research](https://wellcomecollection.org/works/ztn635y7). Humoral explanations are historical positions, not present medical guidance.

### 19. [Relativity](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b02144gl) · 2013-06-06
**Agreement does not require one universal clock.** Relativity can be reconstructed through light signals and differently moving observers, without formulas or confusing relativity with relativism.
Connection direction: Operational time + light -> relative simultaneity -> spacetime.
[Topic research](https://www.einstein-online.info/en/relativity_space_time/). Observer-dependent measurements are constrained, not arbitrary opinions.

### 20. [Bergson and Time](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/m0004s9w) · 2019-05-09
**Measured time and lived time are different questions.** Bergson opens a genuine disagreement that need not be settled by one discipline defeating the other. Memory and anticipation can transform duration.
Connection direction: Clock time versus experienced duration; comparison with fiction is a teaching juxtaposition unless documented.
[Topic research](https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/bergson/). Do not use lived duration to refute the empirical content of relativity.

### 21. [Surrealism](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/p00547l1) · 2001-11-15
**Ideas can be combined artistically.** Dream, chance and a familiar object in an impossible setting make an intelligible artistic operation. Freud, Marx and Dada are more fertile sources than “add art”.
Connection direction: Optical realism + dream association -> a surreal image; reason does not simply vanish.
[Topic research](https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/surrealism). Freudian inspiration is documented; art does not prove psychoanalytic theories.

### 22. [Jorge Luis Borges](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b0076182) · 2007-01-04
**A library can become a philosophical machine.** Borges permits a genuinely different kind of combination: identical words in a changed context, a library with every possible book, a map that defeats its purpose.
Connection direction: Archive, classification, possible worlds, time and unreliable authority recombine as fiction.
[Topic research](https://www.poetryfoundation.org/poets/jorge-luis-borges). No quoted story text; no claim that Borges predicted quantum physics or the internet.

### 23. [Lévi-Strauss](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b01sjjxl) · 2013-05-23
**Relations can matter more than isolated objects.** Lévi-Strauss is a direction for investigating how categories and contrasts organize meaning, with the limitations of the outsider’s scheme left visible.
Connection direction: Classification -> relational structures -> contested universal patterns.
[Topic research](https://www.college-de-france.fr/en/chair/claude-levi-strauss-social-anthropology-statutory-chair). Specific structural claims and source communities need further primary-text verification.

### 24. [Nietzsche's Genealogy of Morality](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b087rt4z) · 2017-01-12
**Ask where a value came from.** Genealogy changes the question from whether a rule sounds timeless to how it acquired its authority and whom it serves.
Connection direction: Inherited moral categories -> historical formation -> later critiques of knowledge and power.
[Topic research](https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/nietzsche-moral-political/). Do not sanitize Nietzsche’s elitism or make genealogy equivalent to “all morality is false”.

### 25. [Complexity](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b03ls154) · 2013-12-19
**The whole can behave unlike any part.** Feedback and interaction can connect economy, ecology and future systems without asserting one universal theory of everything.
Connection direction: Simple local rules -> unplanned patterns; prediction and intervention become different tasks.
[Topic research](https://www.sfipress.org/books/foundational-papers-in-complexity-science). Emergence does not guarantee stability, fairness or governability.

### 26. [The Antikythera Mechanism](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/m0024x0g) · 2024-11-14
**A model can be built into matter.** The Antikythera mechanism makes a powerful return of the oldest sky records: recurring celestial events represented in a working arrangement of gears.
Connection direction: Recorded cycles -> mechanical model -> later clocks and computation, with gaps acknowledged.
[Topic research](https://antikythera-mechanism.namuseum.gr/en/what-is-the-mechanism-and-what-does-it-consist-of/). Do not invent an unbroken device lineage to modern computers.

### 27. [The Fable of the Bees](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/m0000t3y) · 2018-10-25
**Private motives and public outcomes can diverge.** Mandeville creates a provocative counterweight to ancient virtue and later economic order. Keep prosperity, moral cost and distribution as separate questions.
Connection direction: Luxury and self-interest -> unintended social effects; Smith is not just Mandeville with a new label.
[Topic research](https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/mandeville/). Attributed controversial thesis, not proof that greed is good.

### 28. [Scepticism](https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b01kblc3) · 2012-07-05
**Suspending judgment is a possible result.** A researcher need not reconcile two arguments prematurely. Skepticism makes a useful live tile and a continuing constraint on future certainty.
Connection direction: Conflicting appearances -> suspended assent -> demands for evidence.
[Topic research](https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/skepticism-ancient/). Not generic denial and not a claim that every proposition has equal support.

## Selection discipline

The scan considered the entire catalogue rather than searching only for the names in the brief. Military/political events and single-author literary episodes were not rejected as uninteresting; most offered fewer immediate recurring intellectual connections for this particular game. Highly technical mathematics episodes were not selected merely to expand the existing calculation-heavy route. Familiar philosophers can still belong in Atlas without each requiring an episode slot. Likewise, a selected direction may contribute only a tool, a live objection or a cross-chapter return rather than its own scene.

## Evidence limits

The catalogue confirms bibliographic identity, not what speakers said. The linked topic sources support selected background claims at their stated scope; some are directions for deeper primary-source checks, explicitly marked. Every implemented historical connection will need a separate transmission/adaptation/comparison classification and source ledger. The existing Atlas and all saved identities remain unchanged.
